1514355.steps:
step 1, Configure a new interface X4 with zone and IP in IPv4 interface page, and then switch to IPv6 page, give X4 an global IPv6 address;
step 2, Navigate to Network->Routing, switch to IPv6 page, enable OSPFv3 on X4, click OK button ;
step 3, Change router-id to 10.10.10.10, click OK button, connect a router to X4 (OSPFv3 default router-id is 10.0.0.1, and the two neighbors can not use the same  router-id, so its better to change router-id at the first time, to avoid the confiliction.);
step 4, Enable debug OSPFv3 on router, check is there any OSPFv3 packets send from DUT;
step 5, check the OSPFv3 status LED on GUI;
step 6, show OSPFv3 neighbor in CLI, enter zebos, use command "ARS OSPFv3>show ipv6 ospf neighbor" to show the neighbors.

