1514359.steps:
step 1, Configure a new interface X4 with zone and IP in IPv4 interface page, and then switch to IPv6 page, give X4 an global IPv6 address;
step 2, Configure interface X2, connect it to another router B, config router B, enable RIPng and redistribute static routes;
step 3, Navigate to Network->Routing, switch to IPv6 page, enable RIPng on X2, click OK button ;
step 4, Navigate to Network->Routing, switch to IPv6 page, enable OSPFv3 on X4,check option "Redistribute Rip Routes", click OK button ;
step 5, Check DUT routing table, DUT learned ipv6 routes from router B via RIPng, metric is 120, check DUT RIPng database, enter zebos, use command"ARS RIPng>show ipv6 rip database ", it will show all ipv6 routes learned via RIPng;
step 6, Check OSPFv3 database, enter zebos, use command"ARS OSPFv3>show ipv6 ospf database external", it will show AS-external-LSA;
step 7, Check router's IPv6 ospf routes;

1514360.steps:
 step 1, Configure a new interface X4 with zone and IP in IPv4 interface page, and then switch to IPv6 page, give X4 an global IPv6 address;
