1514364.steps:
step 1, Add a vlan sub-interface, parent interface X4, id: 868, zone LAN, ip-assignment: static, input IP address, and switch to IPv6 page, set IPv6 static address;
step 2, Navigate to Network->Routing, enable OSPFv3 on X4:V868, enable redistribute connected routes and static routes;
step 3, Connect cisco router g0/1 to X4, edit vlan 868 on g0/1, enable OSPFv3 on it, redistribute static routes;
step 4, Check OSPFv3 status on X4:V868, the LED is GREEN, and moused over it, it will show the neighbor's info;
step 5, Check routing table on DUT, X4:V868 can learn static routes from router, the metric is 110;
step 6, Check routing table on cisco router, it can learn static routes from DUT, the metric is 110;
step 7, Check the packet monitor on DUT, X4:V868 will send OSPF and process OSPF message.

